  image https://www.w3.org/cms-uploads/_920xAUTO_crop_center-center_none/banner1.jpg "TPAC 2026 is from 26 to 30 October, in Dublin, Ireland. Join us in person or online."
  col
    h2 TPAC 2026
    text TPAC 2026, our major hybrid event of the year, gathers our community on 26-30 October, in Dublin, Ireland.
    text During this exciting week, W3C work groups meet to coordinate work that advances web standardization. TPAC also brings together the W3C governing bodies (Board of Directors, Advisory Board, Technical Architecture Group and the W3C Advisory Committee).
    link "Visit the TPAC 2026 website" https://www.w3.org/news-events/tpac/2026/
row
  col
    h2 Web standards
    text Web standards are the building blocks of a consistent digitally connected world. They are implemented in browsers, blogs, search engines, and other software that power our experience on the web.
    text W3C is an international community where , full-time , and the public work together to develop web standards.
    link Members /membership/list/
    link staff /staff/
    link "Learn more about web standards" https://www.w3.org/standards/
