row
  col
    h3 Improved thread navigation in W3C's mailing list archives
    text A new feature is available in W3C's mailing list archives, aiming to make it easier to read and navigate message threads.
    text Blog
  col
    h3 Introducing group activity pages
    text W3C groups now have an Activity page that shows, month by month, their charters, publications, meetings, participants and GitHub work in one place. The pages are in beta, and we would like your feedback.
    text Blog
  col
    h3 We’re on a roll - EPUB 3.4 is coming
    text The Publishing Maintenance Working Group at W3C has been quietly working on yet another update for the EPUB3 standard, and we're excited to share what we have been up to. Our goal is to not only maintain the EPUB standard, but do our best to keep it in line with the needs of industry, and this update does exactly that. Your existing books do not need to change, if they conform to previous EPUB versions, they will conform to EPUB 3.4. Content you create today will automatically conform as well.
    text Blog
  col
    h3 What’s new in the W3C Website Design System
    text A significant update to the W3C Website Design System was published at the end of September 2026. Here’s what changed and why.
    text Blog
